cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the SituationCatch-Bench diagnostic, please cite it as below."
title: "Situation engineering for reliable evidence use in artificial intelligence (SAGE / SituationCatch-Bench)"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and diagnostic benchmark for situation engineering:
  the explicit construction and validation of the query-relative world state
  that governs evidence applicability. Includes SituationCatch-Bench (4,200
  items across seven applicability categories), the deterministic generator and
  evaluation harness, an integrity-audited single-family Gemini E5 pilot with
  direct/structured/situation prompts plus retrieval (RAG) and agentic
  baselines, and item-level raw responses.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lim
    given-names: Geunsik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1845-7132"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leemgs/sage"
license: MIT
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
keywords:
  - situation engineering
  - evidence applicability
  - situation blindness
  - trustworthy artificial intelligence
  - hallucination
  - temporal reasoning
  - question answering
  - benchmark
  - large language models
